From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicolai Buchwitz <nb@tipi-net.de>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 20:59:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: bcmgenet: collapse TX priority queues to a single queue

The strict-priority TX queues can starve under multi-queue load and
trip NETDEV WATCHDOG. The multi-queue design was originally used for
STB use cases that are no longer needed (confirmed by Justin Chen at
Broadcom). GENET v1 already exercises a single-queue path. Point v2-v5
at the same configuration: ring 0 takes the full BD pool.

Posted to net-next (reviewed by Justin Chen and Florian Fainelli):
  https://lore.kernel.org/netdev/20260612205915.3156127-2-nb@tipi-net.de/

That series only changes bcmgenet_hw_params_v2/v3/v4 because later
kernels share the v4 table with v5. Linux 6.12 still has a separate
GENET_V5 array slot, so this backport also sets v5 (Raspberry Pi 4 /
CM4 / BCM2711).

Tested upstream on Raspberry Pi CM4 (BCM2711). Baseline kernel trips
NETDEV WATCHDOG within seconds under iperf3 UDP saturation
(-u -b0 -P16 -t60). After the change the same test completes without a
watchdog.

Fixes: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/20570

Signed-off-by: Nicolai Buchwitz <nb@tipi-net.de>
[6.12: hw_params is still an array; also set GENET_V5]
Signed-off-by: Stuart Johnson <stuart@stu.org.uk>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/genet/bcmgenet.c | 16 ++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/genet/bcmgenet.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/broadcom/genet/bcmgenet.c
@@ -3743,8 +3743,8 @@ static struct bcmgenet_hw_params bcmgenet_hw_params[] = {
 		.words_per_bd = 2,
 	},
 	[GENET_V2] = {
-		.tx_queues = 4,
-		.tx_bds_per_q = 32,
+		.tx_queues = 0,
+		.tx_bds_per_q = 0,
 		.rx_queues = 0,
 		.rx_bds_per_q = 0,
 		.bp_in_en_shift = 16,
@@ -3760,8 +3760,8 @@
 		.flags = GENET_HAS_EXT,
 	},
 	[GENET_V3] = {
-		.tx_queues = 4,
-		.tx_bds_per_q = 32,
+		.tx_queues = 0,
+		.tx_bds_per_q = 0,
 		.rx_queues = 0,
 		.rx_bds_per_q = 0,
 		.bp_in_en_shift = 17,
@@ -3779,8 +3779,8 @@
 			 GENET_HAS_MOCA_LINK_DET,
 	},
 	[GENET_V4] = {
-		.tx_queues = 4,
-		.tx_bds_per_q = 32,
+		.tx_queues = 0,
+		.tx_bds_per_q = 0,
 		.rx_queues = 0,
 		.rx_bds_per_q = 0,
 		.bp_in_en_shift = 17,
@@ -3798,8 +3798,8 @@
 			 GENET_HAS_MDIO_INTR | GENET_HAS_MOCA_LINK_DET,
 	},
 	[GENET_V5] = {
-		.tx_queues = 4,
-		.tx_bds_per_q = 32,
+		.tx_queues = 0,
+		.tx_bds_per_q = 0,
 		.rx_queues = 0,
 		.rx_bds_per_q = 0,
 		.bp_in_en_shift = 17,
